or":"#C05746"},{"label":"David","color":"#B07CD4"},{"label":"New covenant","color":"#E4DFCE"},{"label":"Unassigned","color":"#5A6178"}],"relkinds":[{"key":"quoted-in","label":"Quoted in","color":"#E8C15A","strong":true},{"key":"fulfilled-in","label":"Fulfilled in","color":"#D9715C","strong":true},{"key":"parallels","label":"Parallels","color":"#6E9BD1","strong":false},{"key":"illustrates-doctrine","label":"Illustrates doctrine","color":"#9B8AD1","strong":false},{"key":"part-of-covenant","label":"Part of covenant","color":"#5FBFA0","strong":false}],"counts":{"topics":5,"portals":0,"edges":4,"relations":0,"outbound":0},"nodes":[{"id":"bt_book_hag","p":0,"x":56,"y":109,"s":-1,"g":6,"bk":"HAG","ty":"BOOK_OVERVIEW","t":"Haggai: overview","d":"Haggai's four messages in the second year of Darius to Zerubbabel and Joshua and the remnant: build the LORD's house, take courage for its glory, receive blessing from this day, and the LORD's choice of Zerubbabel.","q":"Can {{name}} say what Haggai calls the people to do and name two of the messages?","ev":["Name the four dated messages (1:1, 2:1, 2:10, 2:20)","Say what the first message asks (1:8)"],"pp":[[36,1,1,15],[36,2,1,23]],"tier":null},{"id":"bt_hag_consider_your_ways","p":0,"x":56,"y":239,"s":0,"g":6,"bk":"HAG","ty":"STORY","t":"Consider your ways: build the house","d":"Haggai tells Zerubbabel, Joshua and the people that it is not time to live in panelled houses while the LORD's house lies waste; they sow much and gain little, and when they obey the LORD says he is with them and stirs them to work.","q":"Can {{name}} retell what the people were told in Haggai 1 and what they did?","ev":["Say what the LORD says is wrong in 1:4 and 1:9","Describe how the people responded (1:12-14)"],"pp":[[36,1,1,15]],"tier":null},{"id":"bt_hag_glory_of_latter_house","p":0,"x":244,"y":239,"s":0,"g":6,"bk":"HAG","ty":"THEME","t":"The glory of the latter house","d":"The LORD tells the builders to be strong, for his Spirit remains among them according to the word covenanted when they came out of Egypt; he will shake the nations and fill the house with glory, greater than the former, and give peace in this place.","q":"Can {{name}} explain how the LORD encourages the builders in Haggai 2:1-9?","ev":["Read 2:3-5 and say how the LORD encourages them","Describe the promise of 2:6-9"],"pp":[[36,2,1,9]],"tier":null},{"id":"bt_hag_unclean_offering_blessing","p":0,"x":56,"y":369,"s":1,"g":6,"bk":"HAG","ty":"THEME","t":"Holy and unclean; blessing from this day","d":"Haggai asks the priests whether holiness or uncleanness spreads by touch and applies the answer to the people and their offerings, recalls their failed harvests, and says that from the day the temple foundation was laid the LORD will bless them.","q":"Can {{name}} retell the questions Haggai asked the priests and the promise that ends the section?","ev":["Retell the two questions to the priests (2:12-13)","Say what changes 'from this day' (2:18-19)"],"pp":[[36,2,10,19]],"tier":null},{"id":"bt_hag_zerubbabel_signet","p":0,"x":244,"y":369,"s":1,"g":6,"bk":"HAG","ty":"THEME","t":"Zerubbabel the signet","d":"On the same day as the blessing the LORD says he will shake the heavens and earth and overthrow the thrones of kingdoms, and promises to take Zerubbabel his servant and make him as a signet, for he has chosen him.","q":"Can {{name}} tell what the LORD promises Zerubbabel in Haggai 2:23?","ev":["Say what the LORD says he will do to kingdoms (2:22)","Say what he promises Zerubbabel (2:23)"],"pp":[[36,2,20,23]],"tier":null}],"edges":[[1,0,0],[2,1,1],[3,2,0],[4,2,0]],"rel":[]}
